I found no nearest-neighbor violation. Neither universal bound is proved. The [full report](<./P2_REPORT.md>) contains the derivations, assumptions, and remaining obstructions.

The main results are:

1. SU(2)-invariant spin-1/2 chains are settled using the supplied Heisenberg infrared result. Schur’s lemma forces \(h=aI+bP\). The antiferromagnetic sign gives \(k=1,c=1\); the ferromagnetic sign has quadratic excitations.

2. A representation-theoretic sufficient condition covers level-matched fusion families. Write \(s(R)\) for the sum of the highest weights’ Dynkin labels, including multiplicities. I proved
   \[
   \operatorname{ind}(R)\ge s(R),
   \qquad
   \sum_a k_a\le s(R)
   \ \Longrightarrow\
   \sum_a c(G_{k_a})\le d-1.
   \]
   This establishes both bounds for rectangular SU(N) fusion chains conditional on their full infrared identification as \(SU(N)_k\). The level identification itself is not derived here.

